# cc-loop

Orchestrator only — not a coding agent. Loop: `state → planner → task graph → worktree → implementer → tests → reviewer → merge/retry/stop` (sequential graph nodes by default; parallel is opt-in).

**Version:** 0.12.0 · **Integration:** [docs/INTEGRATION.md](docs/INTEGRATION.md) · **Task graph:** [docs/TASK_GRAPH.md](docs/TASK_GRAPH.md) · **Recovery:** [docs/RECOVERY.md](docs/RECOVERY.md) · **Migration:** [rust/docs/MIGRATION.md](rust/docs/MIGRATION.md)

## Tests

```bash
make test
# or: cd rust && cargo test --workspace
```

Contract tests: `rust/crates/cc-loop-contract-tests`. Graph/unit tests live in `cc-loop-core`. Real git in temp dirs — do not mock git.

## Layout (`rust/`)

| Crate | Role |
|-------|------|
| `cc-loop-cli` | `cc-loop` binary |
| `cc-loop-core` | config, state, git, providers, orchestrator, inspect/summary |
| `cc-loop-contract-tests` | black-box CLI contract tests |

Key modules in `cc-loop-core`: `orchestrator` · `inspect` · `summary` · `parallel` · `recovery` · `repair` · `prompt_cache` · `task graph` · `providers/*`

## CLI surface (do not break without INTEGRATION.md update)

`init` `doctor` `list` `status --json` `summary --json` `graph --json` `auto --detach` · `--task-id` on run/resume/status/auto/graph · `CC_LOOP_STATE_ROOT`

Global `--state-root` must precede subcommand.

Operational: `stop`, `cancel`, `cleanup`, `report`, `eval`, `export`. Advanced: `graph --history`, `allow_parallel_execution` / `max_parallel_nodes`.

## Invariants

- `shell=false`; never `pkill -f`
- Process-group kill for timeout cleanup
- No merge on failed/skipped tests (unless `allow_merge_without_tests`)
- Default success is handoff (`auto_merge=false`); merge is opt-in
- `require_distinct_reviewer=true` by default; writer ≠ reviewer
- `auto` requires `test_command` unless `allow_merge_without_tests`
- Never switch user's main checkout
- Dirty repo blocks run; bounded `max_review_patch_bytes` for reviewer
- `claude-code` planner/reviewer: `print_only=true`
- Persist raw provider output even on parse failure
- Legacy state without `task_graph` must load; planner legacy JSON wraps to single-node graph

